Message-ID: <AABAAB0B27AF5C418FE809F352FB7BA4083CA069@023-DB3MPN1-081.023d.mgd.msft.net>

The parameters controlling the node width and height are called iwidth and
iheight. You will have to set those before you do the layout:
g <- randomGraph(V, M, 0.5)
nodeRenderInfo(g) <- list(iwidth=list(a=0.2, d=1.5))
g <- layoutGraph(g)
g <- renderGraph(g)

iwidth and iheight control the size of the rectangular bounding box around
a node, so for symmetry you may want to change both (circles as node
shapes are forced to be symmetric, but boxes or ellipses are not. Also
there is an interaction between the node label size and the node size, and
I think you may have to explicitly set the font size for the node text to
make this work.
Hope that helps,
Florian

-- 






