Dear John,

Thanks for supplying example data.  I have committed a fix an hour ago to 
edgeR 3.0.4.  Using the fixed package, the code I give below runs on my 
laptop using your data in a few seconds.

Two additional comments.  First, we warn in the edgeR User's Guide 
(Section 2.5.6) against using estimated counts from cufflinks or eXpress.

Secondly, your data seems to have some serious quality issues.  An MDS 
plot plotMDS(predFC(y)) shows that samples con3, con4 and case3 are 
massively different from the other samples.  The batch effect will not 
correct for this.  The data shows very large dispersion values.  So I 
don't think you will get good results from the code below, even though it 
runs now without errors.

Best wishes
Gordon

> library(edgeR)
> x <- read.delim("eXpress_Effective_Counts_Example.txt",row.names=1)
> group <- 
factor(c("c","c","c","c","case","case","case","case"),levels=c("c","case"))
